cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "VoxelTrace: vendor-neutral quantitative PET comparability, provenance and trial audit"
abstract: >-
  Research prototype that checks, before analysis, whether quantitative FDG PET/CT
  measurements can be compared across timepoints, scanners and sites under explicit,
  source-cited rule sets (QIBA, EANM, PERCIST), with deterministic preflight, strict SUV/SUL,
  hash-bound human review of reference regions and lesion targets, and immutable evidence
  bundles. Not a medical device; not for clinical diagnosis.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Raymond
    family-names: Confidence
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ConfidenceRaymond/VoxelTrace"
keywords:
  - PET
  - quantitative imaging
  - FDG
  - multicentre trials
  - quality control
  - provenance
